quran[8]{c,v,t}:
  7,44,The people of Paradise will call out to the people of Hell: ‘We have indeed found what our Lord had promised us to be true. Have you (also) found what your Lord had promised (you) to be true?’ They will answer: ‘Yes.’ Then a caller will announce among them: ‘The curse of Allah be upon the wrongdoers—
  7,45,"those who bar (others) from the way of Allah and seek to make it crooked, and they disbelieve in the Hereafter.’"
  7,46,"There will be a barrier between them (i.e. Paradise and Hell). And on the Heights (of that barrier) will be some people who will recognise each of them by their marks. They will call out to the people of Paradise: ‘Peace be upon you!’ They will not have entered it, though they would be eagerly hoping so."
  7,47,"When their eyes will be turned towards the inmates of the Fire, they will say: ‘Our Lord, do not place us among the wrongdoing people.’"
  7,48,"And the people of the Heights will call out to certain men whom they will recognise by their marks: ‘Your accumulation of wealth (or being greater in number) did not avail you, nor did your behaving arrogantly."
  7,49,"Are these (believers) the ones you swore Allah would not bestow mercy upon?’ (Now these people are being told:) ‘Enter Paradise! You shall have no fear, nor shall you grieve.’"
  7,50,"The people of Hell will call out to the people of Paradise: ‘Pour on us some water, or (give us) any of the sustenance Allah has granted you.’ They will say: ‘Allah has indeed forbidden both (of these bounties) to the disbelievers,"
  7,51,"those who took their religion for play and amusement, and whom the life of the world had deceived.’ So today, We forget them, as they forgot the meeting of this Day of theirs, and as they used to deny Our revelations."
